CloudBurrow patch 65 to github.com/goccy/googlesqlite v0.3.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1548). Applies after patch 0061.

Patch 0036 named the change table's flag of a DELETE that is half of an
UPDATE _CHANGE_IS_FOR_UPDATE, and patch 0063 gave a table with a column
of that name no change table. BigQuery reserves only the prefixes
_CHANGE_TYPE, _CHANGE_TIMESTAMP and _CHANGE_SEQUENCE_NUMBER
(https://cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/schemas, "Column names", read
2026-10-17), so such a column is the table's own, and its history must
be kept. The flag is now _CHANGE_TYPE_FOR_UPDATE, under the reserved
prefix _CHANGE_TYPE, which no BigQuery table can have; patches 0036,
0041, 0044 and 0063's statements and tests name it so, and a table with a
column _CHANGE_IS_FOR_UPDATE has a change table with that column among
the table's. A change table made before this patch keeps its history:
the catalog's first sync of a database renames its flag, in SQLite
(ALTER TABLE ... RENAME COLUMN, which renames it in the table's
triggers) and in its catalog spec.

